## What is embalming?

Embalmment preserves the body of your loved one by removing any fluid from their corpse and replacing it with chemicals that inhibit decomposition—a process called “embalming.” Embalmers use various tools to accomplish this task, including needles or syringes which they insert into different parts of the body (such as arms). Once injected inside someone’s remains with these fluids/chemicals—their bodies will no longer decay over time like normal humans do when we die naturally;
